{
 "id": "004",
 "title": "A connector must be followed by a clause",
 "defect": "'A. after', 'A. then' and 'A; ; then' were accepted. After a full stop the new row is empty, so a connector token falls into the no-op branch (prefix 'after'/'before'/'then' are legal at the start of a clause) and nothing records that the clause it announces never arrived. Found by the adversarial suite.",
 "hypothesis": "If every connector token (then/and/next, after, before) writes a PEND mark on the row it announces (once per row), and the row validity layer flags PEND on a row with no action, then a connector that is not followed by an action is rejected, while connectors followed by a clause cost nothing.",
 "affected": "row field PEND (new, marker); B units w_PEND_SEQ, w_PEND_AFTER, w_PEND_BEFORE; V unit dangling_pending.",
 "mathematical_effect": "w_PEND_c = relu(x_c - rp_PEND) writes 1 at most once per row (it is gated by the row's current PEND, read after the reset). dangling_pending = relu(PEND - sum ACT) is 1 exactly when the row announces a clause but holds no action.",
 "expected": "tests/next/defects-004.jsonl: all rejected (was: all accepted). Dev set and earlier suites unchanged.",
 "targets": [
  "tests/next/defects-004.jsonl"
 ],
 "regression": [
